      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Von Recklinghausen disease usually involves the large vessels. Involvement of the pelvic vessels has not been previously reported in the literature. The authors report the case of a man presenting with acute pelvic pain secondary to rupture of an aneurysm of the internal obturator artery, in a context of Von Recklinghausen disease."},
